notes: "This is the scientific worked example: the Dickerson–Drew DNA dodecamer, PDB 1BNA. The plot measures C1′–C1′ distances at twelve paired positions within one deposited structure. It is not an experiment run by HUANDENG, not independent replicates, and not a set of hydrogen-bond lengths. The chart is an original measured figure kept in the asset library; the structure is drawn from the same coordinates. On the next page, this page's Story says what an edit must preserve."
